OL,3,GNEWSA'What terminal cancer has taught
OL,4,Ame about life'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA man living with terminal cancer says
OL,7,Fhis biggest regret is spending decades
OL,8,Fcarrying childhood trauma without
OL,9,Frealising it was shaping his life.
OL,11,FRex Mackrill, 65, from Tetbury,
OL,12,FGloucestershire, says being diagnosed
OL,13,Fwith incurable prostate cancer forced
OL,14,Fhim to reflect on what matters most,
OL,15,Fand one lesson he wished he learned
OL,16,Fearlier: to relish the joy of every
OL,17,Fmoment.
OL,19,F"I knew there was something wrong. I
OL,20,Fknew there was a blackness that I was
OL,21,Fcarrying and I didn't know what it was,
OL,22,Fand I wish I'd known earlier," he said.
